Arguments:
  (none)

Description:
  This command lets you change your personal signature.

  The signature can be used when you write texts that are forwarded to
  external networks, such as Usenet and FTN. It is stored in your personal
  SklaffKOM configuration and can be changed at any time.

  The standard SklaffKOM editor is used to edit the signature.

Note:
  The signature is not the same thing as your Unix .plan file. The .plan
  file is used by, among other things, the classic Unix finger service and
  is changed with the "Change plan" command.

  If you cancel the editor, no changes are saved.

